// cwe_611_unfired.strata -- T-0189 (T-0153 review follow-up) per-CWE
// litmus, design-finding fixture: CWE-611 (Improper Restriction of XML
// External Entity Reference) is cataloged with `capability_kind=None`
// (`_threat.py::CWE_CATALOG`'s own comment: "a parser-configuration
// precondition -- an XML parser resolving a DOCTYPE-declared external
// entity, not a `may` atom KIND the charter's capability-instantiation
// table lists"). No `may` atom can ever drag this obligation in -- the
// same structural gap as CWE-22/CWE-352/CWE-798 (docs/strata/threat.md
// #the-litmus-coverage-cwe-22352798-never-fire-by-design, now extended
// to CWE-611). This fixture models a foreign caller reaching a
// document-parsing node precisely to prove the negative: THREAT003
// reports ZERO CWE-611 obligations here. No hardened twin: there is
// nothing to discharge when nothing fires.
//
// tested end to end (parse -> elaborate -> check_discharge_completeness)
// by tests/unit/strata/test_litmus_cwe.py, which asserts this NON-firing
// explicitly rather than skipping the id.

module cwe_611_unfired

node client : foreign { clearance Public; }
node xml_parser : trusted {
    clearance Internal;
}

flow f_upload : client -> xml_parser { label Public; }
